        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the perpendicular height be $h$ metres. It divides the base into two lengths of $\\frac{x}{2}$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2+\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2&=x^2\\\\h^2&=x^2-\\frac{x^2}{4}\\\\h^2&=\\frac{3x^2}{4}\\\\h&=\\frac{\\sqrt3x}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe area is\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12bh\\\\A&=\\frac12\\times x\\times\\frac{\\sqrt3x}{2}\\\\A&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}x^2\\text{ m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
